I cached the `profile` pointer in a local so the bounds check and field lookup use one stable base pointer, avoiding a repeated member load. This keeps the same validation and return behavior while giving the compiler a slightly tighter access path.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const auto p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return p->fields[profileIndex].num;
}
```